      "notes": "mikefarah yq v4 on its own library (pinned in go.mod): yq expression syntax, eval per document or eval-all over every document, input format from -p or the first file's extension (unknown is YAML), output format from -o (-j is json) or else the input's; YAML output keeps comments, key order and styles. -i evaluates into the first file and publishes it at the captured revisions through the write door. Environment, load and system operators are disabled; -s split files, --from-file and colour output are not supported. Errors print \"Error: ...\" and exit 1. Both yq dialects are served: a python yq spelling (-y, -Y, -c, -s, -S, -a, -R, --tab, --arg, --argjson, --slurpfile, --rawfile, --args, --jsonargs, --raw-output0, --stream) selects python yq, which runs the jq program over each file's YAML documents with jq's statuses and diagnostics, prints jq's JSON unless -y/-Y asks for YAML, and with -i rewrites each file; otherwise yq is mikefarah yq v4. Spellings both dialects share (-e, -n, -r, -i, --indent) mean the same in each; -j stays mikefarah's --tojson.",
